TEXT 112 32 Left 3 ;#172 Op amp gain bandwidth product
TEXT 112 96 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UooUGC7tNRg
TEXT 112 144 Left 2 ;Stepping the feedback resistor through Alan's three values shows that closed-loop gain multiplied by bandwidth stays constant.
TEXT 112 760 Left 2 !.ac dec 200 10 3Meg
TEXT 112 792 Left 2 !.step param RFEEDBACK list 1k 10k 100k
TEXT 112 824 Left 2 !.meas ac Av FIND mag(V(out)) AT=100
TEXT 112 856 Left 2 !.meas ac BW WHEN mag(V(out))=Av*0.7071 FALL=1
TEXT 880 760 Left 2 ;Alan's test circuit: a 1 k input resistor, a 2.2 k load,
TEXT 880 792 Left 2 ;and a 3.9 k/3.9 k divider holding the LM358 at
TEXT 880 824 Left 2 ;mid-supply on a single +5 V rail.
TEXT 880 856 Left 2 ;RF of 1 k, 10 k and 100 k gives 0, 20 and 40 dB.
